This project is a new, clean-room implementation of the word alignment models of eflomal:

  eflomal, https://github.com/robertostling/eflomal
  Copyright Robert Östling and contributors. Licensed under the GNU GPL v3.

  Robert Östling and Jörg Tiedemann (2016). Efficient Word Alignment with Markov Chain Monte
  Carlo. The Prague Bulletin of Mathematical Linguistics 106, 125-146.

  Robert Östling (2015). Bayesian Models for Multilingual Word Alignment. PhD thesis,
  Stockholm University.

No eflomal source code is included in this repository, and none was used to write it. The
implementation follows the papers above and eflomal's public documentation (README and --help).
eflomal was used only as a black-box binary, to compare output quality and performance.
